dialect protocol
protocol s.stdio.semio.image.snapshot
version 1
schema s.stdio.semio.image
start body
framing record

# ARTIFACT-SYSTEM-OVERHAUL-REAL-CODECS-RUNTIME-REUSE-EVOLUTION image wave: REAL binary pack frame,
# replacing the old `serde_json::to_vec`-in-envelope shortcut (`📸️snapshot/🦀️component.rs`'s old
# `ArtifactPack::encode_pack_with`). `format u8` (real, fixed) then `schema_len`/`schema_bytes`
# (real, varint-length-prefixed UTF-8 — matches `write_str_lp`'s own wire exactly, via the proven
# BARE `segment <name> <type>` form: consecutive bare segment lines auto-merge into one segment),
# then `width`/`height` (real fixed `u32` LE), `colorspace`/`bit_depth` (real fixed `u8`) are
# genuinely, fully described. Past that, `icc` (an `Option<Vec<u8>>`) and `frames`/`metadata`
# (HOMOGENEOUS but variable-length repeated records — the `protocol-array-of-records` gap: `repeat`'s
# own arms are tag-dispatched, not "repeat N times, N from a count field", for an untagged
# homogeneous record) are modeled as one opaque trailing `payload` chain, the same honest boundary
# every P1-P3/W-S pilot's own nested/recursive payload uses. The real Rust
# `encode_image_snapshot_binary`/`decode_image_snapshot_binary` (`../../🦀️component.rs`) stays
# genuinely, fully structured (varint counts, per-field length-prefixes, real `u32` LE numeric
# fields) — round-trip tested independently by this facet's own tests, only the protocol
# DESCRIPTION stops at this boundary.
header fixed 1
field format u8

segment schema_len varint
segment schema_bytes Array(u8, Field(schema_len))
segment width u32
segment height u32
segment colorspace u8
segment bit_depth u8

chain payload bytes
